## Summary

Implemented **`DET.DATA.COLOR_ONLY`** as a deterministic accessibility check aligned with the catalog rule: *meaning must not be conveyed by color alone (pattern/label redundancy where detectable)*.

### What the check detects

| Signal | Detection |
|--------|-----------|
| **KS token swatches** | `.ks-swatch` without a `.ks-swatch-label` (≥2 chars) |
| **Chart legend swatches** | `.lenses-overview-donut-swatch`, `.ks-swatch-box`, and other swatch/legend-mark selectors inside chart/legend/table contexts without sibling text, `aria-label`, or `title` |
| **Heatmap-style table cells** | `td`/`th` with a visible background color, empty text, no `aria-label`, inside a table with labeled headers |

Scans are limited to **data contexts** (charts, legends, tables, figures, `.ks-swatch`) to avoid flagging decorative UI chrome.

